Steps

1. Put artifacts to deploy in maven artifactory 
https://[hostname]/ads/download

archetype, import maven plugin, foundation, build-maven-plugin, annotaion jar

example:
mvn deploy:deploy-file -DgroupId=com.ibm.decision -DartifactId=maven-archetype-external-library -Dversion=14.1.10 \
-Dpackaging=jar -DrepositoryId=central -Durl=[target_url] -Dfile=maven-archetype-external-library-14.1.10.jar \
-s settings.xml

2. Fill needed value in settings.xml. 

3. Generate pom for source library and adsLibrary

sample:
mvn archetype:generate -DarchetypeGroupId=com.ibm.decision -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-external-library \
-DarchetypeVersion=14.1.10 -DgroupId=com.cencora \
-DartifactId=adsUtility \
-Dversion=1.0-SNAPSHOT \
-Ddependencies=com.cencora:droolLibrary:1.0-SNAPSHOT \
-Dlocales=en_US \
-DimportMethods=true \
-B -s settings.xml 

4. Generate source code file system structure.
For proper ADS verbalization, use @PureFunction from 
import com.ibm.rules.engine.annotations.PureFunction;
to annotate the needed customized functions in source java file

5. Build and deploy project to artifactory.

mvn clean install -s settings.xml
mvn deploy -s settings.xml

6. Connect ADS to the maven repository

https://[hostname]/ads/admin-platform

7. Import library inside ADS project using pom information.

8. In decision, add dependency, use the verbalization.

Note:
1. These libraries need some development team work to be supported in ADS.
com.bazaarvoice.jolt.Chainr;
com.bazaarvoice.jolt.JsonUtils;



